  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="Inner West Local Environmental Plan 2022">
      <data key="d0">Inner West Local Environmental Plan 2022</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Inner West Local Environmental Plan 2022 is a regulatory framework that outlines building height controls, floor space ratio controls, setback requirements, and parking requirements for residential and commercial developments in the Inner West area.&lt;SEP&gt;The Inner West Local Environmental Plan 2022 is a regulatory framework that outlines building height controls, floor space ratio controls, setback requirements, and parking requirements for residential and commercial developments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-065c424b168a4972c8483e38860e056c</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022_API.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756185287</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Residential Buildings">
      <data key="d0">Residential Buildings</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Residential buildings are defined within the local plan and must adhere to specific height restrictions and parking requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Residential buildings are structures used for housing that must adhere to specific height and space regulations under the Inner West Local Environmental Plan 2022.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-065c424b168a4972c8483e38860e056c</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022_API.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756185287</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Commercial Buildings">
      <data key="d0">Commercial Buildings</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Commercial buildings are structures intended for business activities that are subject to height limitations in mixed-use zones under the Inner West Local Environmental Plan 2022.&lt;SEP&gt;Commercial buildings, according to the local plan, are subject to height restrictions, particularly in mixed use zones, necessitating compliance with established regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-065c424b168a4972c8483e38860e056c</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022_API.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756185287</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Mixed Use Zones">
      <data key="d0">Mixed Use Zones</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Mixed use zones are areas where both residential and commercial buildings are permitted, with specific regulations on building height and floor space ratios.&lt;SEP&gt;Mixed use zones are designated areas where both residential and commercial developments may occur, with specific height and floor space ratio restrictions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-065c424b168a4972c8483e38860e056c</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022_API.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756185287</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Community Contribution Schemes">
      <data key="d0">Community Contribution Schemes</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Community contribution schemes allow for additional floor space ratios in residential and mixed-use developments as part of regulatory planning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-065c424b168a4972c8483e38860e056c</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022_API.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756185169</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Floor Space Ratio Controls">
      <data key="d0">Floor Space Ratio Controls</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Floor Space Ratio Controls refer to regulations that dictate the allowable density of building development in certain zones, specifically outlining the maximum floor space ratio for residential and mixed-use areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Floor space ratio controls specify the maximum allowable floor area relative to the size of the land parcel for both residential and mixed-use developments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-065c424b168a4972c8483e38860e056c</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022_API.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756185287</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Setback Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Setback Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Setback Requirements are the regulations that determine the minimum distance buildings must be set back from property boundaries, ensuring adequate space and compliance in residential development.&lt;SEP&gt;Setback requirements dictate the minimum distance structures must be set back from property boundaries to ensure adequate space and privacy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-065c424b168a4972c8483e38860e056c</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022_API.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756185287</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Parking Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Parking Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Parking Requirements specify the amount of parking spaces that must be provided in residential developments, including standards for visitor and accessible parking.&lt;SEP&gt;Parking requirements stipulate the minimum number of parking spaces needed for residential developments and visitor parking based on the number of dwelling units.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-065c424b168a4972c8483e38860e056c</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022_API.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756185287</data>
    </node>
    <node id="R1 Zone">
      <data key="d0">R1 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The R1 Zone is a residential zoning category under the Inner West Local Environmental Plan 2022, which has specific regulations for building height and floor space ratio.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-065c424b168a4972c8483e38860e056c</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022_API.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756185287</data>
    </node>
    <node id="R2 Zone">
      <data key="d0">R2 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The R2 Zone is another residential zoning category under the Inner West Local Environmental Plan 2022, with its own regulations regarding height and floor space ratio.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-065c424b168a4972c8483e38860e056c</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022_API.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756185288</data>
    </node>
    <node id="B4 Zone">
      <data key="d0">B4 Zone</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The B4 Zone is a mixed-use zoning category in the Inner West Local Environmental Plan 2022 that allows for both residential and commercial development with specific controls on floor space ratio.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-065c424b168a4972c8483e38860e056c</data>
      <data key="d4">Inner_West_LEP_2022_API.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1756185288</data>
    </node>
